# Styling Guidelines

## TailwindCSS v4 Custom Colors

### Color Usage Rules

**❌ NEVER use hardcoded hex colors in className:**

```tsx
// Wrong
<div className="text-[#1a1a1a] bg-[#ffffff]" />
```

**✅ ALWAYS use custom colors defined in [main.css](/src/assets/css/main.css):**

```tsx
// Correct
<div className="text-dark bg-white" />
```

### Color Naming Convention

Always use semantic color names based on actual color values, not context:

**✅ Good naming:**

```css
--color-black: #000000;
--color-white: #ffffff;
--color-gray-200: #ebebeb;
--color-gray-300: #d9d9d9;
--color-gray-400: #c5c5c5;
--color-gray-600: #3f3f46;
--color-gray-800: #1a1a1a;
--color-red-500: #ef4444;
--color-blue-600: #2563eb;
```

**❌ Bad naming:**

```css
--color-pricing-bg: #ebebeb;  // Use --color-gray-200 instead
--color-button-text: #1a1a1a;  // Use --color-gray-800 instead
--color-primary-dark: #123456;  // Use actual color name like --color-blue-800
```

### Adding New Colors

Add colors to [main.css](/src/assets/css/main.css) in the `@theme` section:

```css
@theme {
  /* Use proper color naming */
  --color-gray-100: #f3f4f6;
  --color-blue-500: #3b82f6;
  --color-red-400: #f87171;
}
```

