## Responsive Design Rules

1. **Never use fixed max-width pixels:**

   ```tsx
   // Wrong
   <div className="max-w-[1440px]" />

   // Correct
   <div className="container mx-auto" />
   ```

2. **Use responsive breakpoints:**

   - `sm:` - 640px and up
   - `md:` - 768px and up
   - `lg:` - 1024px and up
   - `xl:` - 1280px and up
   - `2xl:` - 1536px and up

3. **Container approach:**
   ```tsx
   <div className="container mx-auto px-4 md:px-6 lg:px-8" />
   ```

## Height Calculations

When creating full-height sections below fixed headers:

```tsx
// Account for header height (4rem)
<section className="h-[calc(100vh-4rem)]" />
```

## TailwindCSS Best Practices

### Class Ordering

Always follow consistent class ordering for maintainability:

1. Layout (position, display, flex, grid)
2. Sizing (width, height, padding, margin)
3. Typography (font, text)
4. Colors (background, text, border)
5. Effects (shadow, opacity, transform)
6. States (hover, focus, active)

```tsx
// Good
<div className="relative flex w-full h-24 px-4 py-2 text-lg font-bold text-gray-800 bg-white rounded shadow hover:bg-gray-100" />

// Avoid random ordering
<div className="text-gray-800 px-4 relative bg-white w-full hover:bg-gray-100 flex rounded py-2 h-24 shadow font-bold text-lg" />
```

### Use Single Quotes

Always use single quotes for className attributes:

```tsx
// Good
<div className='flex items-center' />

// Avoid
<div className="flex items-center" />
```
